# How long each workspace package's suites take in the package-suites job, in
# seconds, so `.github/scripts/run-package-suites.ts` can split them over the
# shards by weight instead of by count. One package per line: `<package>  <seconds>`.
#
# Every shard reads this file from the checkout and computes the split alone, so
# the file must never come from a cache or a previous run: two shards holding
# different weights would run a package twice or not at all.
#
# A package not listed here costs 5 seconds (DEFAULT_WEIGHT_SECONDS), which is
# what the ~160 small contract and process packages measured on average. Only
# packages of 20 seconds or more are listed, so the file stays short.
#
# Measured as the median of package-suites runs 39365033127, 39361384457,
# 39357729994 and 39357260279 on main (all eight shards green in each).
# To refresh: open a green main run's package-suites job summaries, paste the
# "Measured seconds" blocks of all eight shards here, and sort by seconds.

